{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths","id":1556189,"title":"Whay do werewolves know about the Lower Depths?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-05T13:24:09-08:00","id":1556189,"title":"Whay do werewolves know about the Lower Depths?","content":"Uratha can't naturally access the Underworld, but they know for a fact it exists, just outside their normal range.<br /> <br /> What knowledge'd they have concerning the Lower Depths would they have, considering Maeljin are native to there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:24:16-08:00","id":1556193,"title":"","content":"Anyone can naturally access the Lower Depths, even if this is a hard and dangerous trip. Both Avernian Gates and the Rivers have mundane means to cross them, as you can have the Key for a Gate and the payment for the ferryman, for example.<br /> <br /> On top of that, there are Avernian Gates in the Shadow, usually near places where Death spirits dwell as they're regulars in the Underworld. So Werewolves actually do have more means to learn about the Underworld and its Lower Depths than most other people without specialized means to explore the place. And it is possible that there <b>are</b> specialized means for them to explore the place in the form of Gifts and other resources. The books are not an exhaustive list of every power in the setting, it isn't unreasonable to think most splats have a few tools to do so somewhere in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:26:16-08:00","id":1556194,"title":"","content":"True. Egyptian werewolves probably had a fairly good picture of Duat, and modern Bale Hounds probably possess some juicy, sanity-cracking cosmological secrets...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:27:25-08:00","id":1556195,"title":"","content":"Oh, and to specify. The Underworld and the Lower Depths aren't the same place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:29:49-08:00","id":1556196,"title":"","content":"On average? Likely nothing. For those that actually specialize on looking into it? Potentially quite a lot.<br /> <br /> It's like how many real world human beings have in-depth knowledge of quantum scale reality. Beyond the fact that none of us can just go there to learn about it directly, only a small handful of people have the knowledge and training to even start to comprehend how it works despite most people knowing that quantum mechanics is a thing in science and probably have some vague (and likely very incorrect) about what that means via pop culture exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T14:55:47-08:00","id":1556200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths#post1556189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What knowledge'd they have concerning the Lower Depths would they have, considering Maeljin are native to there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't even know if the Maeljin are actually singular or plural entities and the Lower Depths are a broad class of cosmological phenomena that largely can't be returned from and contain a number of escaping natives that can lie with impunity about the nature of their home. The place beyond the Wounds is a consistent mystery besides strongly-hedged equivalence to the Inferno, which looks different to everybody who takes a traumatic peek into an open Hellmouth. Duat is likewise functionally only accessed through deathly astral projection, and the place the most powerful Strix can open a gateway too is full of the darkest of shadows.<br /> <br /> Dave Brookshaw summed up the category as &quot;off the map and wants to eat us&quot; for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T20:23:11-08:00","id":1556219,"title":"","content":"There's not much universal to be known about them, considering how varied and numerous they are (described as &quot;countless&quot;) and with the only ones labeling them Lower Depths not surviving trips to them. It's entirely possible there's lodges of werewolves walking in and out of them every weekend.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lower Depths are a catch all for these vague other worlds where Awakened won't survive. All one needs is some dots to have mechanical knowledge in them in general, or a specific one if you want. But they aren't really explored in second edition books using Awakened terminology, though there are mentions of other worlds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Misspoke, left out a 'not' before 'surviving trips to them.' 12-06-2025, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T21:13:01-08:00","id":1556221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556195#post1556195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and to specify. The Underworld and the Lower Depths aren't the same place.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, I have a tendency to confuse the Lower Depths with the Lower Mysteries...<br /> <br /> Yet this doesn't change much. The point is less knowing about the Lower Depths and more knowing of a place that isn't a part of known cosmology, because that's all the Lower Depths are in the end, realms whose relationship to the cosmos as a whole is unknown and where Magic faces problems.<br /> <br /> As long as you have a concept of a cosmos with &quot;measurable&quot; realms, you have a concept similar enough to the Lower Depths, while the full concept only really matters to Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T22:00:24-08:00","id":1556223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556219#post1556219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not much universal to be known about them, considering how varied and numerous they are (described as &quot;countless&quot;) and with the only ones labeling them Lower Depths surviving trips to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surviving trips to the Lower Depths is the exact opposite of what prompts the label to be applied to a place whose nature is inferred from it being on the other side of a rift that leaches fundamental concepts from the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556221#post1556221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is less knowing about the Lower Depths and more knowing of a place that isn't a part of known cosmology, because that's all the Lower Depths are in the end, realms whose relationship to the cosmos as a whole is unknown and where Magic faces problems.<br /> <br /> As long as you have a concept of a cosmos with &quot;measurable&quot; realms, you have a concept similar enough to the Lower Depths, while the full concept only really matters to Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lower Depths are places that mostly annihilate anyone with the misfortune to cross into them. Not for nothing does Mage 2e's term for an Iris into the Lower Depths thematically rhyme with Werewolf's term for the metaphysical damage that increase entropy and summon demonic servitors.<br /> <br /> <br /> They're various types of Hell. Some of them are more weird than malicious, but the corruptive effects of their entrances and denizens on the world are the important things for Werewolf, because the Uratha have a well-established tendency to reframe things in familiar terms even if many of the denizens in question weren't sporting lie-enhancement powers or flatly non-communicative. If a particular Depth has interfered with the area before, there may be sources of lore to hunt down (or at least aftermath to scour through); otherwise, the pack gets the unenviable job of finding out what's going on reactively or through ethically iffy probing methods.<br /> <br /> The Maeljin are the usual suspects when it comes to demonic interference, but there's also the outside chance a celestial convergence drops something like the Tutor in the middle of a residential area and everyone has to figure out how to deal with something that reflexively consumes people's sense of self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:06:43-08:00","id":1556258,"title":"","content":"I would assume ancient Egyptian werewolves had a good inkling of Duat, considering the nature of Arisen. Yes, most Arisen fled Egypt in the wake of Unas' fall and the start of the Cannibal Hymn, but a few must've certainly stayed---especially Shuankhsen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T07:11:13-08:00","id":1556293,"title":"","content":"Assuming that nobody returns from the lowers depths because that can not, rather than because they do not want to, maybe they are wonderful heavenly places where those who escape are actually pushed out as a punishment and are twisted and monstourous as a result... Or maybe one of the Lower Depths is like this, because we don't know enough about them to suggest generalising is fair.<br /> <br /> But if we assume that the things which escape are representative of what is in them, then the one thing we know for certain is that things can escape... So returning must be possible, if one can survive (and still want to return).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T07:42:39-08:00","id":1556295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556293#post1556293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if we assume that the things which escape are representative of what is in them, then the one thing we know for certain is that things can escape... So returning must be possible, if one can survive (and still want to return).</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary examples of &quot;visiting&quot; a Lower Depth and &quot;returning&quot; \u2014 mummies and the Hounds of Annwn \u2014 involve functional astral projection/dream journeys with an established relation to the plane in question.<br /> <br /> The primary example outside of that context is &quot;an Infernal demon changes from a corrupted spirit/ghost/Goetia to a true demon after it has descended to the Inferno.&quot; Getting out of the Inferno in this state is largely a function of projecting a tiny piece of themself to steer occultists toward empowering and summoning them.<br /> <br /> If you can't get out of a place that consumes or twists aspects of reality that people need to live through its denizens and the periphery of its entry points without becoming a denizen, that does not paint a picture of Lower Depths being subject to the kind of selection bias that affects most Earth-dwelling changelings' view of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Natives of a place with no concept of e.g. electricity aren't guaranteed to suffer a critical existence failure from emerging into material reality the way humans or anything else with bioelectricity would from going to a place where the laws of physics don't allow them to live. &quot;Things from Plane B can come to Plane A and survive&quot; does not imply &quot;Things from Plane A can come to Plane B and survive to return to Plane A.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T10:41:09-08:00","id":1556303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556295#post1556295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary examples of &quot;visiting&quot; a Lower Depth and &quot;returning&quot; \u2014 mummies and the Hounds of Annwn \u2014 involve functional astral projection/dream journeys with an established relation to the plane in question.<br /> <br /> The primary example outside of that context is &quot;an Infernal demon changes from a corrupted spirit/ghost/Goetia to a true demon after it has descended to the Inferno.&quot; Getting out of the Inferno in this state is largely a function of projecting a tiny piece of themself to steer occultists toward empowering and summoning them.<br /> <br /> If you can't get out of a place that consumes or twists aspects of reality that people need to live through its denizens and the periphery of its entry points without becoming a denizen, that does not paint a picture of Lower Depths being subject to the kind of selection bias that affects most Earth-dwelling changelings' view of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Natives of a place with no concept of e.g. electricity aren't guaranteed to suffer a critical existence failure from emerging into material reality the way humans or anything else with bioelectricity would from going to a place where the laws of physics don't allow them to live. &quot;Things from Plane B can come to Plane A and survive&quot; does not imply &quot;Things from Plane A can come to Plane B and survive to return to Plane A.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I would concur that a Thing from Plane B being able to escape to Place A does not guarantee that a thing from Plane A can survive in Plane B or if they can figure out how to survive (werewolves in this question, possibly mutating/shape shifting/ learning 'gifts' from the local denizens/local spirit? But more generally, things which have some supernatural powers may have some hope of survival...) I am presuppossing that they can figure out how to survive.<br /> <br /> They may not be able to access whatever mechanisms the native use to escape - presumably the entities in question find it difficult to escape in the first place, or they would have over-run the Plane A by now... Or they are so rare in Plane B that them being able to cross freely doesn't make much of a difference population-wise in Plane A? <br /> <br /> I think Dis / the plane where the Strix seem to come from (or go to?) seems like the least impossible to survive and/or escape from, and werewolves might take an interest in the Strix, especially if they were once spirits of humanity (however much they might have changed as a result of whatever happened that made it so people are the only things without spirits).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T11:06:17-08:00","id":1556305,"title":"","content":"As to the Strix,<br /> Dis, as I understand it, lacks vitae. Can a werewolf handle his entire circulatory system catastrophically coming to a halt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T11:14:59-08:00","id":1556306,"title":"","content":"Duat, for instance, lacks Sekhem. Unless somehow magically protected by a powerful effect living things bodily entering Duat instantly die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T14:55:16-08:00","id":1556314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556303#post1556303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I would concur that a Thing from Plane B being able to escape to Place A does not guarantee that a thing from Plane A can survive in Plane B or if they can figure out how to survive (werewolves in this question, possibly mutating/shape shifting/ learning 'gifts' from the local denizens/local spirit? But more generally, things which have some supernatural powers may have some hope of survival...) I am presuppossing that they can figure out how to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have the capacity to learn Gifts <i>as part of the way the Shadow works</i>. As the primary point of reference, on the long list of things Infernal bargains can offer, Gifts and Renown are specifically excluded from what werewolves can get. (Rites and dots of Primal Urge are fair game, but require sacrifices as any other trade does.) Werewolves' adaptability comes from their being shapeshifters who can interface with the spiritual world, whose breadth of purviews is filtered through the spirits that populate it \u2014 it does not translate to carte blanche to derive powers from any type of ephemeral being without the aid of a plot device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They may not be able to access whatever mechanisms the native use to escape - presumably the entities in question find it difficult to escape in the first place, or they would have over-run the Plane A by now... Or they are so rare in Plane B that them being able to cross freely doesn't make much of a difference population-wise in Plane A? </div> </div> </div>The primary examples of how Lower Depths entities escape are that Infernal denizens are occasionally able to exploit people's sins to become a voice in their head that can mildly twist probability around them to steer them toward summoning them in full, fiends in Duat can emerge into the sunlit lands in the presence of depictions of them, and the most powerful Strix in the game can turn an area of complete darkness into a gateway to wherever they're from for a scene, which vampires, ghouls, Strix, and other things with their taint on them can spend a Willpower point to cross into (with the only information on what happens thereafter if they don't cross back over in time being that they're &quot;lost&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Dis / the plane where the Strix seem to come from (or go to?) seems like the least impossible to survive and/or escape from, and werewolves might take an interest in the Strix, especially if they were once spirits of humanity (however much they might have changed as a result of whatever happened that made it so people are the only things without spirits). </div> </div> </div>The suggested divergence point between the Strix and humanity is far enough back in time that it pre-dates the Sundering by an order of magnitude \u2014 we're talking at least 50,000 BCE.<br /> <br /> We shall set aside the matter of local stage hazards in a place of empty darkness for a moment and instead take a moment to remember that this is a place inhabited by Strix, who are not naturally made of ephemeral and can attempt to possess living hosts with moderate Shadow Potency and a point of Willpower \u2014 which paints a rather dire picture whether you interpret the place as full of individual smoke-owls or the unitary source of all the Strix that emerge from its gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T18:26:22-08:00","id":1556325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556305#post1556305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Strix,<br /> Dis, as I understand it, lacks vitae. Can a werewolf handle his entire circulatory system catastrophically coming to a halt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are made to be predators and have shown abilities to do this in the most extreme environments. They were not designed to just be limited to hunting mundane people on the mundane physical world. Like how the Gift of Weather or the Sea offer ways to hunt there, if there is a need to hunt in another world there's no reason to believe there's not something similar available for the determined Uratha hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T19:31:55-08:00","id":1556328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556258#post1556258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would assume ancient Egyptian werewolves had a good inkling of Duat, considering the nature of Arisen. Yes, most Arisen fled Egypt in the wake of Unas' fall and the start of the Cannibal Hymn, but a few must've certainly stayed---especially Shuankhsen!</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than everyone else in Egypt at the time, and all around the world by now.<br /> <br /> Arisen don't usually bring others into Duat or even Neter-Khertet, so they're not really a source of understanding on Duat just for being there. They mostly don't have business there, either, so there's little about them that would increase any splat's likelihood of experiencing those places on their own.<br /> <br /> What they do is that they tell their cults a version of the truth. But it is still just religion in the end, no proof beyond the powers of the Arisen. We can clearly see that at the time this basically meant all of Egypt ended up with a reasonably good idea of what Duat is. Full of flaws, but still quite correct as far as it goes.<br /> <br /> So, Werewolves that <i>believed</i> those religions or followed those cults certainly had a good inkling of Duat, but just as everyone else around them (including other splats). Anything beyond that would require either exceptional Duat related phenomena or someone actually developing specialized powers to access it in some way, and while both are more probable to have happened in Ancient Egypt, this is far from a given, and not something that couldn't happen anywhere else.<br /> <br /> But a lot of things may have been true at some point in ancient Egypt also simply because we're not talking about a particular period, we're talking about a huge span of time that was just as eventful and varied as any other, we just don't have many surviving texts. Think about everything that happened through history since Rome's first Emperor, all the history and wars and changes and whatnot, and then remember this first Emperor is closer to the LLM AI Bubble than to the first awakening of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556305#post1556305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Strix,<br /> Dis, as I understand it, lacks vitae. Can a werewolf handle his entire circulatory system catastrophically coming to a halt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae isn't blood. Living beings do not have Vitae. Vampires and Strix produce Vitae by robbing vitality from living beings.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556306#post1556306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duat, for instance, lacks Sekhem. Unless somehow magically protected by a powerful effect living things bodily entering Duat instantly die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duat does not lacks Sekhem AFAIK, and going there does not <i>destroy</i> Sekhem, nor is it ever said that living beings die upon getting there.<br /> <br /> More importantly, Sekhem is not &quot;life energy&quot;, it has nothing to do with living and everything to do with <i>existing</i> in the firs place, absolutely everything that <i><b>is</b></i> has some Sekhem, even normal objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T21:04:11-08:00","id":1556330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves are made to be predators and have shown abilities to do this in the most extreme environments. They were not designed to just be limited to hunting mundane people on the mundane physical world. Like how the Gift of Weather or the Sea offer ways to hunt there, if there is a need to hunt in another world there's no reason to believe there's not something similar available for the determined Uratha hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) That presupposes that Lower Depths are <i>places</i> with dimensions and shit like that, where the books have been pretty clear that they are, at best, conceptual &quot;spaces&quot;, and at normal are more just an abundant lack of aspects of reality that spit out problems. Even Duat, arguably the most &quot;accessible&quot; of these*, is more a state of psychospiritual ouroborosing, than an actual place.<br /> <br /> 2) If the developers and writers of Chronicles wanted to treat the Lower Depths as actual places you could explore outside of the weird niche cases, discussion about them as places would have been more heartily chased after since 2005 up to the release of the Clade Companion. It's not, because the Lower Depths are, for the most part, not places. At the times they can interact with realities in ways that evokes a sort of trompe-l'\u0153il effect that suggests it, but they're fundamentally nowhere for a werewolf to dive into, let alone ask the question of if Wolf's lineage can better survive reality translation errors crashing programs than they can the depths of space.<br /> <br /> *And keeping in mind only dead people armed by the fallen angels of the shadows of reality's driving impetuses have demonstrated anything remotely resembling successful &quot;exploration&quot; and &quot;navigation&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T04:19:04-08:00","id":1556338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556305#post1556305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the Strix,<br /> Dis, as I understand it, lacks vitae. Can a werewolf handle his entire circulatory system catastrophically coming to a halt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae is not blood. It is the life force which blood carries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T04:25:21-08:00","id":1556339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556330#post1556330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) That presupposes that Lower Depths are <i>places</i> with dimensions and shit like that, where the books have been pretty clear that they are, at best, conceptual &quot;spaces&quot;, and at normal are more just an abundant lack of aspects of reality that spit out problems. Even Duat, arguably the most &quot;accessible&quot; of these*, is more a state of psychospiritual ouroborosing, than an actual place.<br /> <br /> 2) If the developers and writers of Chronicles wanted to treat the Lower Depths as actual places you could explore outside of the weird niche cases, discussion about them as places would have been more heartily chased after since 2005 up to the release of the Clade Companion. It's not, because the Lower Depths are, for the most part, not places. At the times they can interact with realities in ways that evokes a sort of trompe-l'\u0153il effect that suggests it, but they're fundamentally nowhere for a werewolf to dive into, let alone ask the question of if Wolf's lineage can better survive reality translation errors crashing programs than they can the depths of space.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would this contrast with the First hunters? Would Geryo be better able to travel to these places and hunt there? (Even if they wreck the place while doing so)? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *And keeping in mind only dead people armed by the fallen angels of the shadows of reality's driving impetuses have demonstrated anything remotely resembling successful &quot;exploration&quot; and &quot;navigation&quot; </div> </div> </div>Wait, what?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T10:15:00-08:00","id":1556348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556339#post1556339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would this contrast with the First hunters? Would Geryo be better able to travel to these places and hunt there? (Even if they wreck the place while doing so)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans, maybe? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:27:00-08:00","id":1556355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556330#post1556330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the times they can interact with realities in ways that evokes a sort of trompe-l'\u0153il effect that suggests it, but they're fundamentally nowhere for a werewolf to dive into, let alone ask the question of if Wolf's lineage can better survive reality translation errors crashing programs than they can the depths of space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but.<br /> <br /> In this case, but those no-places may inspire an ST to make a chronicle where one or more of them is an actual place. And that happening, there's no real canonical stipulation that they can't be such, so we could say this isn't possible in the setting as described in the books.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say affirmations like that need caveats, and theorizing if a splat can find a way of exploring a Lower Depth is valid. Even exploring no-spaces isn't conceptually new to RPGs, but more directly speaking, as much as the devs think the Lower Depths as just a support effect and not an actual place where action and drama may happen, this is not strictly canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556339#post1556339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would this contrast with the First hunters? Would Geryo be better able to travel to these places and hunt there? (Even if they wreck the place while doing so)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, what?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not &quot;places&quot; something can access in the sense of space, nor can they be wrecked. It's not a matter of not being Material, but literally not being a place. None. Zero.<br /> <br /> Any experience of being somewhere while in a Lower Depth is basically a mushroom trip. Look at how Mummies can't really roll dice during their times in Duat, the &quot;place&quot; doesn't really respond to anything in a physical manner. You can think about it that way: how do you interact with something in the game without dice? Without Traits?<br /> <br /> Oh, and Arisen. She meant the Arisen. They're the angels who &quot;explore&quot; Duat to a given value of &quot;explore&quot;. Although I'd disagree in that I think Duat can and should be explored by anything that manages to pass through the gate. Not that this would result in a trip in any way more real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:29:07-08:00","id":1556356,"title":"","content":"So, in your opinion, thr Lower Depths are 'anti-Supernal Realms', just as much as state of being or frame of consciousness as an actual location?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:55:32-08:00","id":1556359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556356#post1556356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in your opinion, thr Lower Depths are 'anti-Supernal Realms', just as much as state of being or frame of consciousness as an actual location?</div> </div> </div> </div>Collectively they're not even those things.<br /> <br /> Some Lower Depths may be &quot;anti-Supernal&quot;, although I actually doubt, at least in a cosmologically relevant sense. Duat is certainly a &quot;state of being&quot; and a &quot;frame of consciousness&quot;, as you can be there in a way and this removes you from larger reality (so, a state of being), and you can experience it (so, a frame of consciousness). But others, not necessarily.<br /> <br /> Most of them aren't meant to be something you enter and then work within, not even something you experience. You either perceive them in a very limited way or completely indirectly, so while you can decide that in your chronicle they're somewhere you can explore through some means, the games are adamant to stop just short of saying &quot;this is not a real thing and you're just trying to enter the picture in the wall&quot;.<br /> <br /> In a sense they're that, a picture in the wall. It looks like a scene, it seems to have depth, and the figures there seem alive, but ultimately it's just a fine coat of paint on bricks tricking your perception and completely lacking the kind of reality you expect. To be there is not to be transported to the depicted scene, but to be translated into a static blotch of paint in a wall.<br /> <br /> But the specifics, and how much this analogy holds, is a case-to-case analysis. In the end what they have in common is:<br /> <br /> 1- They're phenomena that produces something, and in this sense look like a &quot;place&quot; where those things come from;<br /> 2- Only open to limited or indirect interaction that can't really confirm if they're places or not. <i>Thinking</i> about them as places helps explaining what little we know about them;<br /> 3- Even Mages can't reach them as places and don't know how to properly affect them with Magic, <i>for now</i>. They can't even go there in the way they go to the Astral.<br /> <br /> Nothing else is really guaranteed or common among them, and the ST can give whatever answer they want. But as a matter of fact, the devs didn't intend on making them real places that matter, just things that happen and look like places.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T12:58:37-08:00","id":1556360,"title":"","content":"....that defeats the entire purpose of Duat and Dis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:17:21-08:00","id":1556362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556339#post1556339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would this contrast with the First hunters? Would Geryo be better able to travel to these places and hunt there? (Even if they wreck the place while doing so)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Geryo are locked in the Gauntlet and primarily get out from Reaching out of it in a geographical location or by being given the Siskur-Dah Condition periodically; for much the same reason most werewolves don't usually mess around in the Underworld, it is wildly unlikely that the original kin of the Great Hunter would be tapped to hunt down and kill something that is already dead or so far off the map (physical and conceptual) that it doesn't meet the criteria for auto-tagging by the Geryo's driving purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, what? </div> </div> </div>Mummies, armed by the Shan'iatu, who are rogue servitors of the Judges, who were collectively the reason for the Law of Suffering (i.e. for the most part, living things move in such a way as to avoid or mitigate suffering), being described in Irem's creation myth as salting the earth and turning the primordial seas to blood with their gaze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T13:24:07-08:00","id":1556365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556360#post1556360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....that defeats the entire purpose of Duat and Dis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dis is a practical non-entity. The most detail it gets is speculative based on a legend about the founder of Clan Julii. It's a dark place and there are Owls there. That's the extent of our knowledge and Vampire's placement as a gameline firmly rooted in the material world that's unlikely to change as far as official content is likely to canonize.<br /> <br /> Duat exists as the not-entirely-real space where fiends come from and as the backdrop for the Trials of Duat. It's a vision quest that happens while the Arisen are dead and detached from Time. It is only actually narrative relevant as a thing characters talk about with regards to the commonalities of fiends, the Judges, and what the Arisen can vaguely remember dreaming of when they aren't roused by their cults or their Affinities or the rise of Sothis. 1e managed to go its entire run without worrying about entry in more than abstract terms and 2e's only difference is the introduction of a story-framing minigame between arcs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T14:02:38-08:00","id":1556368,"title":"","content":"....so, Judge avatars rise up from where, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T19:38:07-08:00","id":1556375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556368#post1556368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....so, Judge avatars rise up from where, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same place as fiends: <i>Nowhere that you can visit.</i><br /> <br /> This is not a difficult concept: none of the stuff that comes from Duat does so through an akhet. The dimension does not have any correspondence with Earthly geography and its primary point of entrance is a nonspecific distance in an unbounded cardinal direction through an ephemeral sandstorm in a perspective that puts two omnipresent mountains at the horizons. Its denizens get out by being summoned or depicted or to punish the unfaithful or from interactions with a mummy or from a mummy doing poorly at the tribunal in their soul between incarnations.<br /> <br /> It is, without exaggeration, the closest thing the games have presented to an afterlife, with the only point of argument on that front being that PCs of an appropriate type routinely return from it as part of what they are, when what they are is ritually entombed corpses empowered by their eternal souls and their service to the type of cosmic beings that can get away with splitting their focus between Hell and Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T23:33:05-08:00","id":1556376,"title":"","content":"Or, put another way, <i>nowhere as far as we know</i>.<br /> <br /> There's no meaningful difference between fiends and Avatars coming from somewhere or being actually created when &quot;summoned&quot;.<br /> <br /> Judges are so above everything else most PCs interact with on anything resembling a regular basis that their &quot;presence&quot; in Duat doesn't really mean they're there. Fiends do not necessarily have an existence beyond their interactions with Arisen, as far as anyone knows they &quot;appear&quot; like independent and intelligent entities during the Trials, but this isn't necessarily true. So upon &quot;coming&quot; to the Material, they may very well be actually created whole cloth based on a characterization. Not unlike Hatsumi Miko being made into an hologram or an AI.<br /> <br /> Even if they <i><b>are</b></i> discrete, conscious entities, they may just experience Duat in the same way Arisen do. It's a state of being, but not an actual place, and they don't exist in reality while there. Not Ephemeral Beings that aren't Material in a technical sense, but relate to their reality in a physical, space-based manner, but rather thoughts living in a dream-like state where no interaction is real beyond the memories they create.<br /> <br /> Finally, Duat is literally out of time. Even if it is a place, it isn't a moment. It has no past or future and isn't before or after anything. It doesn't travel through time, it is just timeless, with all perception of sequence being bound to a given Trial. So Fiends and Judges have no past or future either, in an even more radical experience than what Arisen get from a life to the next. So when they exist in the Material, this isn't just possibly one of the few moments they exist in a physical sense, this is certainly their only experience with linear time, if not with time at all.<br /> <br /> So at the end Fiends and Judges exist in such a state that you can't even really test and answer those questions. How can you determine if an entity is discrete and conscious when you can't determine if they really come from a real place, can't define where their experience comes and can't know their relationship with time from a summon to the next?<br /> <br /> All that said, again, nothing is universal or concretely known about Lower Depths. It's not that Duat has no reality, but that <i>we can't know with the current data</i>. At any given chronicle it may be that it is, indeed, a real place, just hard to reach outside strict circumstances, but not impossible, we just don't have a known account of it. Remember that what defined it as a Lower Depth is that we <i>don't know for sure</i> it exists as a place, but it may be. It's still out of time, though, so that's that.<br /> <br /> Dis doesn't have a purpose and I find the whole power to open a passage to it kinda pointless, I'm still to find a good argument for it in the game. The game states in no unclear terms that you can't experience it beyond the very scene the passage lasts and there isn't really much to experience anyway. It's like a sensory deprivation chamber that kills you if you stay. And Strix don't have any meaningful experience from the place, either, that give it any meaning at all. Aside it being a possible source of new Strix that'll be newborns as far as relevant memories go, it doesn't matter as a place, if it is one.<br /> <br /> You can flesh out Dis to your heart's content. In fact you can do anything with it. But if you decide it is nothing and that power just creates a temporary pocket of whatever, it works just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:40:36-08:00","id":1556384,"title":"","content":"Then, did the Shan'iatu cease to exist, upon entering Duat? They were certainly quite existent, prior to the Rite of Return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:09:16-08:00","id":1556389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556384#post1556384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, did the Shan'iatu cease to exist, upon entering Duat? They were certainly quite existent, prior to the Rite of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally impossible to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:27:25-08:00","id":1556391,"title":"","content":"You know, it just struck me: you're describing the Lower Depths <i>exactly</i> the same way more mystically inclined mages believe the Supernal World to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:01:11-08:00","id":1556407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556384#post1556384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, did the Shan'iatu cease to exist, upon entering Duat? They were certainly quite existent, prior to the Rite of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are irretrievably gone from the world as they once were. Their programmed drives in the Rite of Return and whatever hallucinatory encounters the Arisen might remember having with them during the Trials are all that remain of them in the setting as is relevant to a game.<br /> <br /> Everything in Duat is cosmologically black-boxed to a similar degree that you're not going to find the big-picture plans of the God-Machine in terms that aren't decided for an individual Demon chronicle by a given troupe \u2014 for all practical purposes they are figments in the mind of God until something makes them real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556391#post1556391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it just struck me: you're describing the Lower Depths <i>exactly</i> the same way more mystically inclined mages believe the Supernal World to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a reminder, the Inferno \u2014the O.G. Lower Depth in the overall setting's cosmological design timeline \u2014 is populated by beings whose primary point of emergence into reality can readily masquerade as mental illness or stress hallucinations, who are less capable of overt possession than more monomaniacal invisible entities, and who use real people's darker imagination to invent and reify forms and purviews for them to exploit \u2014 they are the classic example of the B-is-to-C-as-A-is-to-B relationship between the Supernal, the Phenomenal, and the Lower Depths because <i>Phenomenal entities describe them the way the Supernal describes the Phenomenal</i>.<br /> <br /> The assorted devils down below also hijack invisible entities susceptible to their corruption, but the whole reason it's wildly ambiguous whether true demons are all individuals, all extensions of one entity, or somewhere in between is because the core of the superstructure(s) that create that ambiguity exist in a place where nobody is remotely guaranteed to return from and everything that comes from there has preternatural capability in the field of lying.<br /> <br /> Mummy deliberately plays a more ambiguous game with regards to whether its high-level supernatural forces are demonic or divine, but what it's not unclear on is that it only becomes more than pictures on the wall by, well, having pictures on the wall out in the real world \u2014 fiends who don't hitch a ride on Sybaris or the Trials travel to the land of the living by way of depictions of their forms, and the Scroll of Ages the Sesha-Hebsu are concerned with is basically just <i>the aggregate of written history</i> (which sees more than one mention in the gameline of needing to have beings wiped from it as a poetic flourish on &quot;this person needs to be put in the dirt so hard nobody will ever know they existed&quot;).<br /> <br /> Bringing it back to Werewolf again, you may notice in Shunned by the Moon that the core issue of the Bale Hounds \u2014 being hard enough to find that their presence is in doubt and engendering paranoia about who to trust \u2014 is shared by the Strix. (You may also recall that There Are No Owls in Seattle.) Bale Hounds communicate with the Maeljin through Soulless Wolf, who is a wolf-shaped hole in the world that cannot leave the Wounds, and Soulless Wolf claims a whole bunch of contradictory things about what it is and how it's related to the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> The book also notes that minor Wounds, while not omnipresent, are far from uncommon, and there are enough young and reckless werewolves in the world that it is unlikely some of them haven't thought about taking the fight to the enemy, which makes it the sort of story beat you would have seen mentioned by now in the books if the Lower Depths were traversable in the sort of way that could return reliable intel, but again: one-way trip for the living and everything that comes out can lie like a rug, particularly since &quot;opening&quot; a Wound is either outside the scope of typical player tools to do so or involves the kind of unreliable or extraordinary means of opening a gateway to Hell described in Inferno or the Clade Companion.<br /> <br /> A werewolf (or pack thereof) who can cross into and out of the Lower Depths to learn more than a sufficiently driven occultist might would be the stuff of legend, because entering the Lower Depths is often broadly synonymous with dying, whether in actual or practical terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:22:59-08:00","id":1556410,"title":"","content":"So, <i>are</i> Wounds connected to a Lower Depth? How does the Maeltinet crawl up from the Inferno? Presumably in the same manner as a fiend or avatar of a Judge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:25:31-08:00","id":1556411,"title":"","content":"And, as a complete side-note, are the Lands of Worms from <i>Bloodlines: The Ageless</i> Wounds? I know the book isn't canon, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T15:25:38-08:00","id":1556416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556410#post1556410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, <i>are</i> Wounds connected to a Lower Depth? How does the Maeltinet crawl up from the Inferno? Presumably in the same manner as a fiend or avatar of a Judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be extremely weird for the newest iteration of the mechanics for Wounds to include several powers that go by the same names and do the same things as demon-specific Dark Numina from <i>Inferno</i> and <i>not</i> have that tacitly signify that <i>Inferno</i>'s statement that for that book's purposes the Maeljin and their servants are Infernal demons still holds true even if the primary named Maeljin Bale Hounds serve have shifted away from the ones corresponding to the seven deadly sins plus Deception and Violence.<br /> <br /> The mechanism by which a Maeltinet emerges from its connected Wound is not described, but just going from the material in Inferno alone there's loads of ways, setting aside how even just becoming Wounded prompts a spirit to discorporate and reform in a Wound without having to spend any discernible time in Hell; the Shadow has its share of spatial shortcuts and Wounds can spread through loci if they're contagious (which in turn means spirits compatible with Wounded resonance can hide in those loci's area of influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556411#post1556411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, as a complete side-note, are the Lands of Worms from <i>Bloodlines: The Ageless</i> Wounds? I know the book isn't canon, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ageless</i> isn't official content, but the Land of the Worms and the Sta-Au bloodline are adaptations of official material from <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i> and <i>Ancient Mysteries</i>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34492-1001-vampire-story-hooks?p=1383279#post1383279\">It may or may not have a tie to another part of the cosmology</a>, but that place is described in a separate part of <i>Summoners</i> than the one that discusses beings from the Lower Depths, instead describing it as &quot;a very specific Underworld.&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1346138-mummy-the-curse-2e-kickstarter?p=1346666#post1346666\">Though there's a bit of a writing history tangle</a> that may leave it ambiguous as to whether the home of the Helminth is a Lower Depth after all, the Land of the Worms is not a Wound for the simple reason that Wounds are taxonomically part of the Shadow and the Land is encountered in the Flesh. They might correspond to Shoals, but they don't seem to have the kind of negative resonance that would attract the servants of the Maeljin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T18:42:40-08:00","id":1556422,"title":"","content":"Well, the reworked Sta-Au seek to become 'perfect predators' by slowing attuning themselves <i>to Twilight</i> and eventually shed their bodies and then journey to monstrous 'paradises'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28921,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","user":"CreatorFounderMaker","date":". 12-10-2025, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T17:12:06-08:00","id":1556448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556391#post1556391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it just struck me: you're describing the Lower Depths <i>exactly</i> the same way more mystically inclined mages believe the Supernal World to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because in both cases we have phenomena that seem like a place, but aren't necessarily so, and we interact with them solely through manifestations in the world. They are defined partially by being unknowable, partially by being sources of things instead of places to explore, partially by being highly abstract. In the end, they are explanations for things that happen without a knowable cause, not places to explore, and what matters to the canon is their effects in the actual realms meant for exploration and on characters' experiences.<br /> <br /> You can otherwise take from that similarity what you will. Most Mages think of them as opposites, like Satchel described, and that's more or less <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WordOfGod\" target=\"_blank\">Word of God</a>. They may actually be the same thing, the Lower Depths being either facets of the known Supernal Realms or hitherto unknown Supernal Realms whose Arcana are special in some way. They may be linked in more unexpected ways or may not be linked at all, just a passing similarity in perception born out of our limitations more than a shared nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556410#post1556410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, <i>are</i> Wounds connected to a Lower Depth? How does the Maeltinet crawl up from the Inferno? Presumably in the same manner as a fiend or avatar of a Judge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably.<br /> <br /> Even if for some reason they're not connected to Hell, they still seem to be connected to a place that may or may not be real, so this is a yes.<br /> <br /> By the very nature of the Lower Depths by their current definition, though, the question is almost unanswerable. If a definitive answer is found, it'll probably be a &quot;no&quot;, or a redefinition of what a Lower Depth is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T09:15:20-08:00","id":1556475,"title":"","content":"And, to continue the Sta-Au point, the version I'm talking about, while <i>not</i> canon is way cooler than the official version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T14:17:51-08:00","id":1556569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556475#post1556475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, to continue the Sta-Au point, the version I'm talking about, while <i>not</i> canon is way cooler than the official version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's a point that needed continuing and this doesn't seem to actually do anything for the topic of the thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> Adding a caveat to distinguish the abilities of the Maeltinet from my earlier note on the limitations of Infernal pacts: Maeltinet in both editions are capable of bestowing Gifts appropriate to their natures in the usual fashion, which nevertheless is separate from granting the ability to enter and survive whatever &quot;world&quot; exists beneath the Wounds (whether that's the Inferno or something else) \u2014 the closest thing we have to that is <i>Zud'nalu</i>'s Envoy of Virukh-Ur ability, and that's an ability given to a Primal Urge 9 Bale Hound as a travel power to facilitate what may be a Contagion-related story-hook rather than ritual scarification to express part of the nature of a werewolf through the lens of the corruption and subversion of the natural order, which we see through void reivers typically results in less extreme unsettling powers like the Gift of Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T14:26:26-08:00","id":1556570,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn. Is Soulless Wolf 'real', then? Is he like some kind of 'anti-spirit'? Why is there no communication from the Maeljin <i>directly</i>? Are the Maeljin even existent, or are they, in your opinion, as 'real' as the Judges of Duat, in that they're less beings and more unholy archetypes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T15:56:21-08:00","id":1556575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556570#post1556570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmn. Is Soulless Wolf 'real', then? Is he like some kind of 'anti-spirit'? Why is there no communication from the Maeljin <i>directly</i>? Are the Maeljin even existent, or are they, in your opinion, as 'real' as the Judges of Duat, in that they're less beings and more unholy archetypes?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Maeljin have consistently been described as ambiguous in the nature and reality of their existence, which puts them at around the same level of confirmed reality as the Chthonic Gods from Geist, who are worshipped and served by Reapers but aren't directly active in the way that the Judges and the Exarchs are \u2014 the Maeltinet are their spawn and it's certainly within the scope of Virukh-Ur's potential claims for the wolf-shaped hole in the world to be their singular-collective avatar making an elaborate pretense of acting as a go-between.<br /> <br /> Even in the event that Soulless Wolf somehow only ever appeared to solitary Bale Hounds, it has a consistent appearance and dispatches shadow wolves that act as its eyes and ears and serve as an indicator of Bale Hound activity in an area beyond the activities of the Asah Gadar themselves, which indicates it's at least &quot;real&quot; in the sense that multiple people can see and recognize it.<br /> <br /> The closest thing there's been to a direct and unambiguous extension of one of the Maeljin so far is the Lady of the Lake, the patron of the Lodge of the Lake from Lodges: the Splintered, who was a fossilized face found in an ice core taken from the largest subglacial lake in Antarctica, whose unwitting Bale Hound servants sometimes hear the name the 1e corebook attributes to the Calipha of Pride whispered on the wind, and who only spoke to those prospective servants one-on-one, all of which is part of a story hook about an apocalyptic event involving the emergence of an archdemon brewing at the ends of the earth \u2014 and considering the type of unreal things that can emerge that far afield from various parts of the cosmology (and the known tendency of Wound-things to lie), that doesn't really guarantee anything in the grand scheme of things re: Are The Maeljin Real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T00:11:02-08:00","id":1556591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556570#post1556570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is there no communication from the Maeljin <i>directly</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no direct communication between the Uratha and the higher powers of the spirit realms. Luna may communicate through ambiguous dreams and lunes but it may just be dreams sent by lunes, and the Firstborn totems have a hierarchy of lesser spirits to transmit their own messages in obscure ways. Between Two Rivers depicts Fenris-Ur searching through Basra and passively gathering Uratha from around the globe to it without any direct communication made. They're not like a manager who might call a subordinate to shoot the shit, they're &quot;the aloof and distant gods of Shadow.&quot; Uratha already aren't human, Maeljin are even further detached from normal socialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-14-2025, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T07:47:43-08:00","id":1556607,"title":"","content":"Ah, I'd forgotten 'bout that...silence...from most Rank 6+ Ephemeral Entities, save for the tribal totems, Luna and <i>VERY</i> rare occasions in which Royal Avatars show up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T10:59:26-08:00","id":1556617,"title":"","content":"Could Soulless Wolf generate a Royal Avatar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T12:06:32-08:00","id":1556621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1556189-whay-do-werewolves-know-about-the-lower-depths?p=1556617#post1556617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could Soulless Wolf generate a Royal Avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're Rank 6 or above they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T13:51:15